    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Two ensemble classifiers were trained and cross-validated on the Telco churn\n",
    "data, across three class-balancing strategies.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data\n",
    "\n",
    "- 7,043 customers, 21 columns. `customerID` dropped as an identifier.\n",
    "- `TotalCharges` coerced from text to numeric: 11 blank strings became nulls.\n",
    "  Every one belonged to a `tenure == 0` customer, so they were filled with 0.0\n",
    "  rather than the median (1,397.48).\n",
    "- `Churn` encoded as `Yes -> 1` / `No -> 0`; 1,869 churners (26.54%).\n",
    "- 15 categorical features one-hot encoded (first level dropped), 3 numeric\n",
    "  features left unscaled.\n",
    "- Stratified 80/20 split: 5,634 training / 1,409 test.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Balancing\n",
    "\n",
    "Three strategies were compared inside the cross-validation pipeline \u2014 no\n",
    "balancing, class weighting (`class_weight=\"balanced\"` / `scale_pos_weight`),\n",
    "and SMOTE \u2014 each with a small `GridSearchCV` grid.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Results\n",
    "\n",
    "See the comparison table above for the ROC-AUC, accuracy, precision, recall and\n",
    "F1 of all six configurations. The ROC curves and confusion matrices are in\n",
    "`reports/figures/roc_curves.png` and `reports/figures/confusion_matrices.png`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Artifacts written by this notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "- `reports/figures/churn_distribution.png`\n",
    "- `reports/figures/numeric_by_churn.png`\n",
